        {
          "text": "I loaded the last crate of milk into Pops’s truck and slammed the tailgate shut. The sound echoed across Marigold Ranch",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 47
        },
        {
          "text": "Five years ago, the ranch would have been covered in pumpkins by now. Orange lights would have been hanging from the fen",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 167
        },
        {
          "text": "Now the porch sat empty. No pumpkins. No lights. No decorations",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 458
        }
      ],
      "words": 85
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Before leaving, I spent nearly an hour in the barn with Blueberry. Like I did every morning. I sat in the corner of her ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1051
        },
        {
          "text": "Blueberry never offered advice. Not that I expected much from a horse, but she listened, and somehow that was enough",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1437
        },
        {
          "text": "I almost lost her after the accident five years ago. While I spent months in hospitals and physical therapy, Pops had tr",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1615
        }
      ],
      "words": 100
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Most people in Willow Creek didn’t know the full extent of my injuries, and that was exactly how Pops and Meme wanted it",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2924
        },
        {
          "text": "What they didn’t know was that I came home missing a leg",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3200
        },
        {
          "text": "Pops always said small towns had a way of turning tragedy into entertainment, and after everything that had happened, ne",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3257
        }
      ],
      "words": 87
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The accident had taken my future, but Pops had helped me survive it. He sat beside me through physical therapy appointme",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4166
        },
        {
          "text": "Then one morning his heart simply gave out. No warning. No chance to prepare or to say goodbye",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4404
        },
        {
          "text": "Some losses change your life. Others change who you are. Losing Pops did both",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4614
        },
        {
          "text": "Losing a leg changed my body, but losing Pops had changed everything else",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4853
        }
      ],
      "words": 69
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "After Pops died, most of the ranch hands left for bigger operations. The dairy cooler needed repairs I couldn’t afford. ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6497
        },
        {
          "text": "Every month felt like plugging holes in a sinking boat with whatever scraps I could find. And every month I wondered if ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6707
        }
      ],
      "words": 93
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Five years ago, I’d spent half my life making fun of this truck. Now it was one of the few things I had left of Pops",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8338
        },
        {
          "text": "The engine sputtered. Once. Twice",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8905
        },
        {
          "text": "As if the morning wasn’t bad enough, the sky finally opened. Rain hammered the roof of the truck so hard I could barely ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10120
        },
        {
          "text": "“Well,” I muttered, reaching for the door handle. “This is going to suck.”",
          "ok": true,
